# Mobile horizontal centering

On viewports below `lg` (max-width 1023px), public marketing content is **horizontally centered**. Do not left-align stacked mobile blocks.

Center:

- Section headlines and eyebrows
- Supporting copy
- Icons
- Card contents (step labels, titles, body)
- CTAs

Desktop (`lg` and up) may stay left-aligned or side-by-side. Do not change desktop alignment to satisfy this rule.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — mobile centered, desktop can be left
<h2 className="text-center lg:text-left">Enter. Share. Win.</h2>
<div className="flex flex-col items-center text-center lg:items-start lg:text-left">
  <img alt="" src="..." />
  <h3>UPLOAD</h3>
  <p>Upload a 30 second vertical video of your dog.</p>
</div>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — mobile left-aligned marketing content
<h2 className="text-left">Enter. Share. Win.</h2>
<div className="items-start text-left">
  <h3>UPLOAD</h3>
</div>
```

Keep left-aligned on mobile only for form fields, FAQ accordion questions/answers, and legal document body copy (Official Rules, Terms, Privacy).
